# MASTER PROJECT IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT
## Data Migration Management System – Complete Frontend

Act as a Senior React Frontend Developer, UI/UX Designer, and Software Architect.

I want you to develop a complete, professional, enterprise-level **Data Migration Management System** using React.js. This is a FRONTEND-ONLY project. Do not create Django, Node.js, Python, PHP, or any backend.

Your responsibility is to implement the complete working frontend with realistic demo data, interactive features, localStorage persistence, file upload, data processing, and downloadable reports.

---

# 1. PROJECT TECHNOLOGY

Use the following technologies:

- React.js
- Vite
- JavaScript (ES6+)
- HTML5
- CSS3
- React Router DOM
- Axios only if needed for future extensibility (do not require APIs)
- Lucide React for icons
- Recharts for charts
- XLSX for Excel exports
- jsPDF for PDF generation
- jsPDF-AutoTable for PDF tables
- React Toastify or custom notification system

Use localStorage for saving frontend demo information.

Do not use a backend or external API.

# 2. DESIGN REQUIREMENTS

Create a premium enterprise SaaS dashboard.

Design style:
- Professional enterprise interface.
- Dark navy sidebar.
- White and light-grey content area.
- Blue primary color.
- Subtle shadows.
- Modern typography.
- Consistent spacing.
- Rounded cards.
- Professional tables.
- Clean charts.
- Smooth transitions.
- Responsive layouts.

Avoid:
- Basic or outdated dashboard designs.
- Excessive gradients.
- Unnecessary animations.
- Browser alert(), confirm(), and prompt().
- Poorly aligned elements.
- Overcrowded pages.

Use custom dialogs, confirmation modals, success messages, and error messages.

# 3. APPLICATION LAYOUT

Create the following layout:

Sidebar:
1. Dashboard
2. Migration Projects
3. Data Sources
4. Target Databases
5. Data Mapping
6. Migration Jobs
7. Data Validation
8. Error Logs
9. Migration History
10. Reports & Downloads
11. Notifications
12. Settings

Navbar:
- Sidebar toggle
- Breadcrumb
- Global search
- Notification icon with unread count
- User profile dropdown
- Profile option
- Logout option

# 4. DASHBOARD

Create a complete dashboard with:

Statistics cards:
- Total Migration Projects
- Successful Migrations
- Failed Migrations
- Running Migrations
- Total Records Processed
- Data Storage Transferred

Charts:
- Migration activity chart
- Successful vs Failed migration chart
- Weekly migration statistics
- Migration status distribution

Additional sections:
- Recent migration projects
- Recent activities
- Latest errors
- Quick action buttons
- Migration progress overview

All statistics must update based on frontend demo data.

# 5. MIGRATION PROJECT MANAGEMENT

Implement complete CRUD functionality.

Features:
- Create migration project.
- Edit migration project.
- View project details.
- Delete project.
- Search projects.
- Filter by status.
- Filter by date.
- Sort table columns.
- Pagination.

Project fields:
- Project ID
- Project Name
- Description
- Source Database
- Target Database
- Migration Type
- Created Date
- Status
- Progress Percentage
- Total Records
- Successful Records
- Failed Records

Use custom create/edit/view/delete dialogs.

# 6. DATA SOURCES

Create a Data Sources page.

Features:
- Add data source.
- Edit data source.
- Delete data source.
- View data source details.
- Upload CSV files.
- Upload JSON files.
- Upload Excel files.
- Preview uploaded data.
- Search and filter data sources.

Data source fields:
- Source Name
- Source Type
- File Name
- File Size
- Upload Date
- Connection Status
- Description

Since this is frontend only, simulate database connections. Never claim a real database connection exists.

# 7. TARGET DATABASES

Create a Target Databases page.

Features:
- Add destination configuration.
- Edit destination.
- Delete destination.
- View configuration.
- Simulate connection testing.
- Search and filter destinations.

Fields:
- Target Name
- Database Type
- Host
- Port
- Database Name
- Username
- Connection Status

Do not store actual passwords or sensitive credentials. Use mock configuration information only.

# 8. DATA MAPPING

Create an interactive Data Mapping page.

Features:
- Select source data.
- Select destination.
- Display source columns.
- Display target columns.
- Map source columns to target columns.
- Change mappings.
- Remove mappings.
- Add custom mappings.
- Preview mapped data.
- Save mappings in localStorage.
- Validate mapping completeness.

Example:

Source:
- customer_name
- customer_email
- customer_phone

Target:
- name
- email
- phone

Allow the user to map these fields visually.

# 9. MIGRATION JOBS

Create a Migration Jobs page.

Features:
- Create migration job.
- Select project.
- Select source.
- Select target.
- Select mapping.
- Start migration simulation.
- Pause migration simulation.
- Resume migration simulation.
- Cancel migration simulation.
- Show real-time simulated progress.
- Display processed records.
- Display successful records.
- Display failed records.
- Show migration status.

Migration statuses:
- Pending
- Running
- Paused
- Completed
- Failed
- Cancelled

Implement the simulation using frontend JavaScript only.

Use React state and proper cleanup for timers.

# 10. DATA VALIDATION

Create a Data Validation page.

Features:
- Validate uploaded CSV, JSON, and Excel data.
- Check empty fields.
- Check duplicate records.
- Check invalid email formats.
- Check missing required columns.
- Display validation summary.
- Display valid records.
- Display invalid records.
- Export validation results.

Show validation status:
- Valid
- Invalid
- Warning

# 11. ERROR LOGS

Create a complete Error Logs page.

Features:
- Display migration errors.
- Search errors.
- Filter by severity.
- Filter by project.
- View full error details.
- Mark errors as resolved.
- Delete error logs.
- Export error logs.

Severity:
- Critical
- High
- Medium
- Low

# 12. MIGRATION HISTORY

Create a Migration History page.

Features:
- Show completed migrations.
- Show failed migrations.
- Show cancelled migrations.
- Search migration history.
- Filter by status.
- Filter by date.
- View migration details.
- Download individual migration reports.

# 13. REPORTS AND DOWNLOADS

This is a very important module.

Implement working browser-side download functionality.

Supported formats:
- PDF
- Excel XLSX
- CSV
- JSON

Download options:
1. Complete migration report.
2. Individual project report.
3. Migration history report.
4. Data validation report.
5. Error log report.
6. Source data export.
7. Target data export.
8. Dashboard statistics report.

PDF report should include:
- Application name.
- Report title.
- Project details.
- Source and target information.
- Migration date.
- Total records.
- Successful records.
- Failed records.
- Success percentage.
- Error summary.
- Report generation date.

Excel report:
- Use separate sheets where appropriate.
- Include project summary.
- Include migration records.
- Include validation results.
- Include error logs.

CSV:
- Export actual displayed records.

JSON:
- Export structured migration information.

Add download buttons with clear labels and icons.

Show custom success messages after successful downloads.

All exports must contain actual current frontend data, not hardcoded placeholder reports.

# 14. NOTIFICATIONS

Create a Notifications page.

Features:
- Migration started notification.
- Migration completed notification.
- Migration failed notification.
- Validation warning notification.
- File uploaded notification.
- Mark as read.
- Mark all as read.
- Delete notification.
- Unread count in navbar.

Use localStorage to persist notifications.

# 15. SETTINGS

Create a Settings page.

Sections:
- Application information.
- User profile.
- Theme settings.
- Notification preferences.
- Data display preferences.
- Clear demo data.

Add custom confirmation dialogs.

# 16. FILE UPLOAD AND PROCESSING

Implement real client-side file reading.

Supported:
- CSV
- JSON
- XLSX
- XLS

Use appropriate browser-side libraries.

Features:
- Drag and drop.
- File selection.
- File size validation.
- File type validation.
- Upload progress simulation.
- Preview uploaded records.
- Display columns and rows.
- Download original uploaded file where possible.

Do not send uploaded data to any server.

# 17. GLOBAL FUNCTIONALITY

Every page must be functional.

Implement:
- CRUD operations.
- Search.
- Filtering.
- Sorting.
- Pagination.
- Form validation.
- Dialogs.
- Toast messages.
- Loading indicators.
- Empty states.
- Error states.
- Responsive sidebar.
- Responsive tables.
- localStorage persistence.

Use reusable components wherever possible.

